# From "Sensing Locale 1" (Wave VI - Odyssey, CD1-1): reaching a non-physical
# arm through an object to touch what's beyond it. Both arms, one at a time,
# in the tape's own order (right, then left).

@segment  sensing-locale-1
@title    Sensing Locale 1
@levels   F12
@duration ~5m

say Become acquainted with your second body — the energy that surrounds your physical body. Take a moment to feel it.
pause 8
say Now notice your right arm. Its position. Your fingers, and the direction they're pointing.
pause 6
say Slowly, just through thought, stretch your non-physical arm out in that same direction. Further and further.
pause 8
say Reach for something familiar, beyond where your physical arm could ever reach. Keep stretching until you feel something.
pause 12
say Straighten your non-physical hand, and gently push against it. A little more. A little harder. Let any resistance give way.
pause 8
say Now reach for whatever's beyond that object — the one your hand just passed through. Feel it. Notice its texture. Take your time exploring it.
pause 10
say Now, calmly, withdraw your hand. Bring it slowly back to your energy body, back to where it started.
pause 8
say Relax, and remember that feeling.
pause 5
say Now the same, with your left arm. Let it extend outward, in the direction it's pointing. Further and further.
pause 8
say Reach for something familiar, beyond your physical reach. Keep stretching until you feel it.
pause 12
say Straighten your hand, and push gently against it. A little more. Overcome the resistance.
pause 8
say Reach for what's beyond it. Feel it. Notice its texture. Explore.
pause 10
say Withdraw your hand now, slowly, back to your energy body.
pause 8
say Relax, and remember the feeling.
pause 6
